This is a 2-gram language model, based on a vocabulary of 3663 words,
  which begins "0-0-1", "0-0-2", "0-0-28"...
This is an OPEN-vocabulary model (type 1)
  (OOVs were mapped to UNK, which is treated as any other vocabulary word)
Good-Turing discounting was applied.
1-gram frequency of frequency : 338 
2-gram frequency of frequency : 69847 15954 6404 3455 2207 1473 1105 
1-gram discounting ratios : 1.00 
2-gram discounting ratios : 0.40 0.56 0.69 0.78 0.78 0.86 0.83 
This file is in the ARPA-standard format introduced by Doug Paul.

p(wd3|wd1,wd2)= if(trigram exists)           p_3(wd1,wd2,wd3)
                else if(bigram w1,w2 exists) bo_wt_2(w1,w2)*p(wd3|wd2)
                else                         p(wd3|w2)

p(wd2|wd1)= if(bigram exists) p_2(wd1,wd2)
            else              bo_wt_1(wd1)*p_1(wd2)

All probs and back-off weights (bo_wt) are given in log10 form.

Data formats:

Beginning of data mark: \data\
ngram 1=nr            # number of 1-grams
ngram 2=nr            # number of 2-grams

\1-grams:
p_1     wd_1 bo_wt_1
\2-grams:
p_2     wd_1 wd_2 

end of data mark: \end\

